  "battle_semantics": "Battle properties live per can_hit FX layer, not per action. Attack props (Explode, Scatter, Pierce, Slash) stack and are visual-only; defence props are mutually exclusive per layer and only \"deflect\" has an engine implementation.",
  "fx_semantics": "fx_layers follow fx-authoring.md. Burst anchors (point, r_hand) are fixed-offset approximations from the character root — no live joint tracking.",
  "activation_trigger_semantics": "Layers activate via trig / trig_ref / trig_delay_ms chains; cycle fields reference layers as \"action_name:LayerID\".",
  "authoring_note": "Authored in Rig Forge. Draw-order/visibility layers are an authoring construct and are not exported; in-betweens are baked into keyframes because the loader plays keyframes as authored with no interpolation.",
  "special_stance": {
    "_comment": "Charged-counter stance (generic engine system, combat.tick_special_stance). Meter: +1 per hit blocked or taken, charges_required fills it. Then frames 0..hold_frame play (attack_special baked frames, 42 total at duration_ms pace), the pose is held hold_ms while braced (hits are blocked, no damage/knockback); a blocked hit plays the remaining frames as a counter with one strike per strike_frames entry. If nothing hits during the hold the remaining frames play out with no strikes. hold_frame is the 0-based index (frame 8 in 1-based terms). strike_frames are the swing peaks (blade-tip speed maxima in the source poses: 22, 28, 32, 39); counter_hit_damage is HP per strike.",
    "charges_required": 5,
    "frames_set": "special",
    "hold_frame": 7,
    "hold_ms": 2000,
    "duration_ms": 2400,
    "strike_frames": [
